Float precision issue
print(1.1 + 2.2 == 3.3)  # False
==, !=, >, <, >=, <=. Always return True or False. Comparing floats can be tricky: 1.1+2.2 != 3.3 in Python due to floating-point precision. String/tuple/list comparison is element-by-element left to right; first differing element decides; if equal length and no differences, they are equal;

